course: dictionary
lesson: 2140
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Coot is one of them. «A coot is a black water bird with a white beak and a white forehead patch» uses the bird meaning, so you can picture it on a pond.
explain: The informal meaning is different. An «old coot» is a funny or slightly rude name for a strange or grumpy old man. Look at the words around it: if the sentence talks about ponds, feet and feathers, it means the bird; if it talks about a person who is grumpy, it means the man.
explain: Ask what the sentence is about, then try each meaning in the sentence. If one meaning makes sense and the other does not, you have found the right one.
fact: «Coot» (noun) means a black water bird with a white beak and a white forehead patch.
fact: Coots live on ponds and lakes in the UK, Europe and Australia.
fact: «An old coot» (informal) means a funny or slightly rude name for a strange or grumpy old man.
fact: «As bald as a coot» (UK) means completely bald, because of the coot's white forehead patch.
fact: A coot has three toes forward and one back, with flat flaps called lobes.
exercise: «In winter, a coot with a white beak and forehead paddled across the pond.» What is a coot in this sentence? | A duck with webbed feet | A grumpy old man | A moorhen with a red and yellow beak | *A black water bird with a white beak and forehead patch
exercise: Grandad says, «Don't mind him, he's an old coot.» What does coot mean here? | A pond with ice on it | A white forehead patch | A black water bird | *A strange or grumpy old man
exercise: «A coot has three toes forward and one back.» How many toes does a coot have facing forward? | *Three | Two | Four | One
test: Which meaning of coot fits this sentence? «The coot dived under the water to find weed at the edge of the lake.» | A kind of pond weed | *A black water bird with a white forehead patch | An old man who is grumpy | A cold winter day
test: Why does «as bald as a coot» mean completely bald? | Because it is a funny name for a bird | *Because of the coot's white forehead patch | Because coots live in caves | Because coots lose all their feathers
exam: «The old coot shouted at the children who played near his garden.» Which meaning of coot fits here? | A pond with ice on it | A white forehead patch | *A strange or grumpy old man | A black water bird with a white beak
